==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Catclaw Castle (Enemy Base)|Catclaw Castle]].
*Infinite [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Dark Otter]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Bun Bun Symbiote]] spawns as the boss.
**8 [[Shibalien Elite]]s spawn, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Star Peng]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**3 [[Dark Otter]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage serves as a check for [[Cats of the Cosmos]] chapter 1 treasures, as without them the Star Pengs are extremely difficult to kill. If you have all Cosmos treasures, this stage will become way easier. Of course all [[Into the Future]] crystals would be needed to make the Bun Bun Symbiote manageable, but with these treasures the enemies will fall relatively quickly.

Use long-ranged Area Attackers such as [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] to keep all of the enemies back, while crowd-controllers like [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer]] can Freeze the majority of threats. [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] and/or [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] both help with taking down the Star Pengs, Dark Otters and Doge Darks (Can Can also gives extra cash if you have their [[Money Up]] [[Talents|Talent]]), while occasional [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cats]] will mitigate bad Bun Bun Symbiote Wave RNG.

==Hints==
This hint only appears as a defeat message that is given after losing the stage.
*Starred Aliens are a tough fight without<br>Treasures from Cats of the Cosmos.<br>If you made it this far, you can definitely<br>find the Treasures! Don't give up!

